Quoth Steve VanDevender <stevev@hexadecimal.uoregon.edu> on this day
of 25 Sep 2003 02:09:16 -0700:

>Perhaps I will have to try the fast deep plunge technique myself.  

Fast deep plunge, if you really mean what you say, is not very wise.
Monster generation depends both on dungeon level and on character
experience level. So you can get deeper without seeing serious nasties
if you're at a low XL; OTOH, once you do see them, you can easily get
killed in one hit.

>I
>have otherwise had only limited success pacing things slow and building
>up my experience before going deep.

Depending on how slow you're going, that can be as foolish as the
"fast deep plunge." If you level up much faster than you descend,
you'll find that you're encountering much tougher monsters on higher
levels, which means you probably haven't had the chance to find good
armor yet, which means you're probably fighting those tougher monsters
without a good AC.

Probably the best strategy, unless you're going for some sort of
challenge, is to clear each level, make sure it's fully explored, and
then descend, regardless of what XL you've arrived at yet. Do some
fighting yourself and let your pet do some fighting. Always be
prepared to run back upstairs if you feel you're in over your head.
Watch your XP when in a fight; don't keep whacking to the death.

